#: core/Mcp/bootstrap.php:23
msgid "Actions provided by PublishPress plugins."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:23
msgid "Move content to a Board status"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:24
msgid "Move an editable Board item to an authorized native status using expected_hash. Scheduling accepts a number of days, weeks, months or years; native publication/date behavior applies. Global schedule defaults remain unchanged. dry_run does not move content."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:33
msgid "Find Planner users, roles and taxonomy choices"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:34
msgid "Find a bounded page of native users, roles, public taxonomies, terms or Permissions groups for Planner filters and notification recipients. Returns identifiers and labels without email/account internals. User lookup requires list_users; groups require the active Permissions integration and its settings capability. Category filters use slugs; general workflow term filters use numeric term IDs."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:42
msgid "Export selected Calendar content"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:43
msgid "Render up to 100 explicitly selected readable/editable Calendar items as native iCalendar text. Does not create a public URL or return feed credentials. Editorial details require the native editorial-field viewing capability."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:52
msgid "Find Planner content"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:53
msgid "Find editable content for Calendar, Content Board or Content Overview. Bounded filters include post type, title search, status, author, taxonomy terms and date range. Every result requires native view and object permissions. Board and overview display configuration is available separately."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:62
msgid "Read a Planner content item"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:63
msgid "Read an editable post with its current revision, native post type/status choices, terms and scheduling dates. Requires the selected Planner view and edit_post/read_post on this object. Passwords and arbitrary metadata are excluded."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:73
msgid "Create or update Planner content"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:74
msgid "Create a draft or update discovered content using native post controllers, author/term permissions and Planner hooks. Existing content requires expected_hash. Changes are a patch; omitted content, authors and terms remain. Dates use ISO 8601 with a time-zone offset. dry_run performs all permission and validation checks without saving or triggering notifications."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:84
msgid "Reschedule Planner calendar items"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:85
msgid "Move up to 50 Calendar items to YYYY-MM-DD dates, retaining each native time of day. Uses Calendar publishing/author permissions and move hooks. All objects and revisions are checked before any writes. dry_run previews the complete batch. A later failure reports already moved IDs rather than pretending the batch was unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:93
msgid "Discover Planner content choices"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:94
msgid "Read native post types, post statuses and taxonomies for an enabled Planner view. Includes object capability names and active Pro editing/integration state. Use these exact identifiers before content writes."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:348
#: core/Mcp/Content.php:351
msgid "Use a valid ISO 8601 publication date."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:405
msgid "This post type does not support the supplied content field."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:441
msgid "Content was saved, but some taxonomy assignments could not be confirmed. Read this object before retrying."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Content.php:447
msgid "Content term assignments could not be confirmed. Read this object before retrying."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Display.php:16
msgid "Read native Planner display values"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Display.php:17
msgid "Read the selected post’s native Calendar information or configured Board/Overview column values as plain text. Uses active dependency renderers and native view/object permissions. Editorial fields require their own viewing capability; protected keys, structured custom metadata, links and form credentials are withheld."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Display.php:24
msgid "Read your Planner view filters"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Display.php:25
msgid "Discover the native filter values and exact input schema for your own Calendar, Board or Overview. Includes active editorial fields, taxonomies and Pro integrations; no other user preferences are read."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Display.php:32
msgid "Save your Planner view filters"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Display.php:33
msgid "Patch your own native view filter values using expected_hash and discovery. Native date, keyword, taxonomy and integration sanitizers apply. Omitted filters remain. dry_run does not save."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Display.php:41
msgid "Find content using native Planner filters"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Display.php:42
msgid "Query a bounded native Planner view using your saved filters or a typed filter patch. Uses the native Calendar/Board/Overview query, including active editorial metadata, taxonomy, Checklists, SEO and Revisions integration filters. Each returned object requires read/edit permission. Does not change saved preferences."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Display.php:52
msgid "Read Planner view configuration"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Display.php:53
msgid "Discover native ordered columns/filters, custom labels and active integration choices for Calendar, Board or Overview. Calendar supports filters only. Native Pro, Checklists, SEO and Revisions filters supply their own choices."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Display.php:60
msgid "Configure Planner columns and filters"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Display.php:61
msgid "Replace one ordered list of native columns or filters using discovered identifiers and expected_hash. Custom metadata keys require explicit labels; credentials and protected security metadata are rejected. Other view settings remain unchanged. dry_run validates without writing."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Display.php:71
msgid "Find custom view metadata keys"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Display.php:72
msgid "Search up to 20 existing metadata identifiers through native Planner discovery. No values are exposed; protected/security keys are withheld."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Display.php:288
msgid "Your view filters changed. Read them again."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Editorial.php:15
msgid "Reorder all editorial fields"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Editorial.php:16
msgid "Replace the order of all native Editorial Fields, supplying every field ID and its current expected_hash from discovery. All definitions are validated before native position updates. dry_run does not write. A failed multi-field update reports confirmed IDs."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Editorial.php:27
msgid "Discover editorial fields"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Editorial.php:28
msgid "Read native Editorial Fields, their exact definition schema, types, dropdown choices, post-type applicability and revisions. Includes checkbox, text, paragraph, number, date, location and user fields."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Editorial.php:37
msgid "Create or edit an editorial field"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Editorial.php:38
msgid "Create or patch a native Editorial Field definition using discovered fields and choices. Existing definitions require expected_hash; existing slug/type cannot be changed because native post values depend on them. Preserves unrelated fields. dry_run validates without creating terms."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Editorial.php:46
msgid "Delete an editorial field"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Editorial.php:47
msgid "Delete one native Editorial Field definition with its current revision. Uses native taxonomy deletion and cache refresh. Existing post metadata follows the native deletion behavior. dry_run checks access without deleting."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Editorial.php:57
msgid "Read a post’s editorial fields"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Editorial.php:58
msgid "Read fields applicable to one editable post, their JSON schemas, native stored values and revision. Requires the filtered editorial-field view capability plus edit_post/read_post. Dates use the native YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM control format; empty values clear metadata."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Editorial.php:65
msgid "Update a post’s editorial fields"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Editorial.php:66
msgid "Patch only supplied native Editorial Field slugs using get-editorial-values discovery and expected_hash. All types, dates, user/role restrictions and dropdown choices are validated before writing. Omitted fields and term counts are preserved. Native zero/empty clearing semantics apply. dry_run previews without saving or firing field-update hooks."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Editorial.php:92
msgid "Supply every editorial field in the desired order."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Editorial.php:165
#: modules/editorial-metadata/editorial-metadata.php:1549
msgid "Editorial field not found."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Editorial.php:174
msgid "Existing field slug and type are fixed by the native data model."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Editorial.php:196
msgid "This editorial field name or slug is already in use."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Editorial.php:322
msgid "Editorial fields changed. Read them again."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:15
msgid "Read Planner dashboard content"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:16
msgid "Read native unpublished status counts or your own followed content. Requires the enabled native widget and edit_posts. Counts additionally require edit_others_posts and read_private_posts; followed items require per-post read/edit access. No other user subscriptions are queried."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:23
msgid "Rotate the Calendar feed key"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:24
msgid "Invalidate existing authenticated Calendar subscription links using the revision from Calendar settings discovery. The new credential is never returned. Requires manage_options and an enabled Calendar. dry_run does not rotate the key."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:35
msgid "Inspect Edit Flow migration status"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:36
msgid "Read a revision and counts for a native Edit Flow migration stage. Raw options, user data and metadata are never returned. User and content permissions are checked for affected objects."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:43
msgid "Run an Edit Flow migration stage"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:44
msgid "Run one native migration stage using expected_hash from status discovery. Affected users and posts must be editable; configuration locks and network permissions apply. dry_run validates without writing. These native stages are not transactional; inspect status after any unconfirmed failure. Stages are bounded to 1000 source records/objects."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:54
msgid "Read the Planner dashboard note"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:55
msgid "Read the native dashboard notepad and its revision. Requires the enabled notepad and native note editing capability."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:62
msgid "Update the Planner dashboard note"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:63
msgid "Update the current native notepad using expected_hash. Native plain-text sanitization and object permission checks apply. dry_run does not save."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:72
msgid "Read Planner diagnostics status"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:73
msgid "Read only the native debug log existence, size and revision. Raw log data, paths, message payloads and credentials are excluded."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:80
msgid "Clear the Planner debug log"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:81
msgid "Delete the native Planner log using its current revision and native capability. No arbitrary path is accepted. dry_run does not delete."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:121
msgid "Metadata migration is locked by site configuration."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:126
msgid "Use native migration administration for datasets larger than 1000 records."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:137
msgid "Resolve conflicting legacy and Planner metadata in native administration first."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:241
msgid "The dashboard note changed. Read it again."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Maintenance.php:267
msgid "The debug log changed. Read it again."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:17
msgid "Read an editorial discussion"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:18
msgid "Read a bounded page of private editorial comments across permitted posts or on one editable/readable post. Cross-post browsing requires edit_posts; search and author_id filters are supported. Returns author IDs and permitted attachment IDs without email/IP/user-agent data. Requires Editorial Comments enabled for this post type."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:25
msgid "Add or edit an editorial comment"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:26
msgid "Add a comment/reply or edit an existing editorial comment through the native lifecycle and notification hooks. Editing requires the native own/others comment capability and expected_hash. Attachments must be readable/editable existing media. dry_run checks without saving, sending notifications or altering files."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:36
msgid "Delete an editorial comment"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:37
msgid "Trash one native editorial comment, or permanently delete an already trashed comment, with expected_hash and own/others deletion capability. Native comments with replies cannot be deleted. dry_run validates without changing the discussion."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:47
msgid "Read post notification followers"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:48
msgid "Read native user, role, group and email follow selections for one editable post. Native email recipient addresses are included only for an authorized editable post. Includes expected_hash for supported follower patches."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:55
msgid "Update post notification followers"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:56
msgid "Patch native user, role, group or email follower lists using expected_hash. Omitted follower selections remain unchanged. Every ID/role is validated before native taxonomy relationship writes. Requires edit_post_subscriptions and object edit/read access. dry_run previews without writing."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:68
msgid "Read user notification channels"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:69
msgid "Read a user’s native workflow channel preferences. Requires pp_set_notification_channel and edit_user for that user. Includes available email/mute and active Pro Slack choices, with no OAuth tokens."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:76
msgid "Update user notification channels"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:77
msgid "Patch native per-workflow user channel choices using expected_hash. Every workflow, channel and user permission is checked before writes. Use email, mute, or Slack when available; Slack destinations require active Pro. Omitted preferences remain. dry_run sends no messages and stores nothing."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:88
msgid "Read Planner delivery status"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:89
msgid "Read a bounded page of native notification log status. Every referenced post/workflow requires object access; cross-site records are excluded. Message bodies, email addresses, raw errors, credentials and cron payloads are never returned."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:96
msgid "Archive or delete selected notification logs"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:97
msgid "Archive or delete up to 50 explicitly selected native delivery logs with their revisions. All permissions and objects are validated before changes. Deletion uses the native model and cancels that log’s associated queued task. dry_run does not cancel or delete anything. Partial failures report completed IDs."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:200
msgid "Some editorial comment changes could not be confirmed. Read this discussion before retrying."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Notifications.php:218
#: modules/editorial-comments/editorial-comments.php:808
msgid "A comment with replies cannot be deleted."
msgstr ""

