#: core/Mcp/Settings.php:15
msgid "Discover Planner features"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Settings.php:16
msgid "Discover Calendar, Content Board, Content Overview, Editorial Fields, Editorial Comments, notifications, dashboard, dependencies and Pro features. Each entry gives its settings schema and native module state. Secrets and license settings are not exposed."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Settings.php:24
msgid "Read Planner settings"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Settings.php:25
msgid "Read one discovered Planner module, exact JSON types, native choices, defaults and its revision. For example calendar, content_board, notifications, editorial_metadata, or Pro reminders/slack."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Settings.php:32
msgid "Update Planner settings"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Settings.php:33
msgid "Patch supplied settings only, using the schema and expected_hash from get-plugin-settings. Native validators and configuration locks apply. dry_run validates without writing. Boolean JSON false is distinct from the string false. Empty lists clear list selections."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Settings.php:41
msgid "Enable or disable a Planner module"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Settings.php:42
msgid "Change one native optional module switch using the revision returned by settings discovery. Mandatory/autoloaded modules cannot be disabled. Feature availability changes after the next request; refresh the AI connection after changes."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Settings.php:65
msgid "Native Calendar feed public visibility disables per-user visibility filters for subscription queries. Enable only when that wider visibility is intended."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Settings.php:129
msgid "Planner module is unavailable in this edition."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Settings.php:208
msgid "Select at least one Calendar post type."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Settings.php:213
msgid "This post type is enabled by site code."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Settings.php:249
#: core/Mcp/Settings.php:285
