#: core/Mcp/WorkflowFields.php:167
msgid "Protected metadata placeholders are unavailable through MCP."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/WorkflowFields.php:236
msgid "Conflicting values for the same native workflow field."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Workflows.php:15
msgid "Discover notification workflow fields"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Workflows.php:16
msgid "Read exact native workflow event, content, receiver, status/taxonomy filter, template and option schemas. Active Pro modules add before/after publishing timers and the network administrator receiver. Use these nested field names before saving; channels are selected in user notification preferences."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Workflows.php:23
msgid "Find Planner notification workflows"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Workflows.php:24
msgid "Find a bounded page of native notification workflows, including title, status and current revision. Requires native notification management and per-workflow access."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Workflows.php:31
msgid "Read a notification workflow"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Workflows.php:32
msgid "Read native workflow configuration and expected_hash, including every supported active step and filter. Internal metadata and authentication credentials are excluded."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Workflows.php:39
msgid "Create or update a notification workflow"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Workflows.php:40
msgid "Create a draft or patch supplied native workflow fields. Existing workflows require expected_hash. Publish only after all configuration writes are verified. Native event/receiver classes persist values. dry_run validates choices, edition, object and content-scope permissions without writes or sending messages. Unconfirmed multi-step writes report the workflow ID and its active state; inspect it before retrying."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Workflows.php:48
msgid "Trash, restore or delete a notification workflow"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Workflows.php:49
msgid "Use native workflow trash, restore and deletion with expected_hash and object permissions. Permanent deletion requires an already trashed workflow. dry_run checks without writing."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Workflows.php:59
msgid "Export Planner notification workflows"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Workflows.php:60
msgid "Export up to 50 authorized native notification configurations in the Planner MCP transfer format. Secrets, license keys and unrelated post metadata are excluded. Use import-workflows for validated copies."
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Workflows.php:67
msgid "Import Planner notification workflows"
msgstr ""

#: core/Mcp/Workflows.php:68
